  <entry>
    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/1506.06940v2</id>
    <title>Approximation of groups, characterizations of sofic groups, and equations over groups</title>
    <updated>2016-06-07T22:39:20Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1506.06940v2" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/1506.06940v2" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>We give new characterizations of sofic groups:
  -- A group $G$ is sofic if and only if it is a subgroup of a quotient of a direct product of alternating or symmetric groups.
  -- A group $G$ is sofic if and only if any system of equations solvable in all alternating groups is solvable over $G$.
  The last characterization allows to express soficity of an existentially closed group by $\forall\exists$-sentences.
  Keywords: sofic groups, approximations, equations over groups.</summary>
    <category term="math.GR" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <published>2015-06-23T11:02:53Z</published>
    <arxiv:comment>The article is supposed to replace 1405.7329. It is based on the same ideas as 1405.7329, but I hope is written more clear and contains more results</arxiv:comment>
    <arxiv:primary_category term="math.GR"/>
    <arxiv:journal_ref>J.Algebra 477 (2017) 147-162</arxiv:journal_ref>
    <author>
      <name>Lev Glebsky</name>
    </author>
    <arxiv:doi>10.1016/j.jalgebra.2016.12.012</arxiv:doi>
    <link rel="related" href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jalgebra.2016.12.012" title="doi"/>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/1002.3082v1</id>
    <title>Almost commuting matrices with respect to normalized Hilbert-Schmidt norm</title>
    <updated>2010-02-16T13:32:01Z</updated>
